harmaceutical and other medical technology partners, such as benchtop testing, preclinical studies, clinical trial support, regulatory consultation, and translation from the preclinical to the clinical setting. It has licenses and collaboration agreements with Koninklijke Philips N.V., UCB Biopharma SRL, Clinical Laserthermia Systems AB, University of California, San Francisco, and NE Scientific, LLC. The company was formerly known as MRI Interventions, Inc. and changed its name to ClearPoint Neuro, Inc. in February 2020. ClearPoint Neuro, Inc. was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Solana Beach, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph Michael Burnett | President, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 172 people. Revenue per employee of $215K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 17%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["ClearPoint Neuro Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $276M market cap on $37M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +23% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -260% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 61% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $24M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -10.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 1.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 66% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 62/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 168% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its lon